  "__comment": "PR_MY_MODULES_V2_SRV/ModuleHeaderSet response (the 'My Courses' page), OData v2 delivered inside a POST $batch — see docs/tss-recon/tss-api-notes.md §PR_MY_MODULES_V2_SRV. Feed verified live 2026-08-19; re-captured 2026-08-21 on the same student, who by then was ALSO WAITLISTED for two courses — rows 4 and 5 are the first real waitlist rows anyone has seen, and they are what settled the parser's rule. Transcribed from the model the page had already loaded (nothing was requested by us), so the $batch envelope is not reproduced here; the extension reads the {\"d\":{\"results\":[…]}} document out of the batch body. Strings/booleans/numbers are wire-verbatim; date fields are omitted because UI5 had already turned the wire's \"/Date(…)/\" into Date objects, and the deferred navigation properties (Exam, ModuleGroup) are omitted as noise. ModregId is a booking-record GUID (PII) and is REDACTED. WAITLIST vs BOOKED, as captured: SmStatus '00' vs '01' · SmStatusText 'Waitlisted' vs 'Booked' · WaitlistBooking true vs false · WaitlistPosition 2 and 11 vs 0 (0 is this feed's empty value, present on every booked row) · SemanticState 'Warning' vs 'Information'. Note also that a waitlisted row leaves ScShort/ScStext empty and AssignedCgTop all-zero.",
